        ],
        "reason": "These are independent omissions of AsyncFunctionDef from classifications that already support FunctionDef. In #401, the scope registry must associate asynchronous definitions with FunctionScope so annotated argument binding does not escape to an inappropriate scope. In #470, the overload recognizer must admit asynchronous source nodes so valid overload declarations receive the existing redefinition exemption. Both fixes extend the responsible classification under Python-3.5 compatibility policy, rather than adding a parent fallback or suppressing diagnostics generally. Ordinary function behavior, decorator identity checks, and unsupported-runtime AST access remain boundaries. The argument-field omission in #507 and alternative-branch omission in #771 require different structural operations and are not included merely because they also concern newer syntax.",
