        "reason": "In #434, a bare overload name imported outside a class is missed because recognition lacks enclosing-scope lookup; the repair searches the reversed scope stack and requires the first binding to be an ImportationFrom for typing.overload. In #561, an aliased module receiver is missed by spelling-based recognition; the repair searches the same lexical ordering and requires the first binding to be an Importation from a supported typing module. The shared causal operation is first-binding provenance resolution, with a nearer unrelated binding preventing recognition of an outer import. This group covers #434's scope-lookup component, not its separate any-decorator change. For #561, the supplied merged implementation and regression support module-alias recognition; they do not establish that every renamed-Literal symptom described in the issue body was corrected.",
