        "reason": "Both defects arise because an existing superficial eligibility condition admits an object that does not satisfy the specialized consumer's data contract. In #422, name membership does not establish that the binding owns import-specific fullName metadata; a short-circuit ImportationFrom check must precede that access. In #674, the name __all__ in module scope does not establish that its immediate parent owns an assignment value; dispatch must require an immediate Assign, AugAssign, or AnnAssign parent before constructing ExportBinding. Their independent fixes strengthen the responsible entry conditions rather than inventing missing attributes or catching the resulting exceptions. Assignment-backed decorators must retain ordinary redefinition diagnostics, and indirect export targets must retain ordinary unused-import diagnostics. Supported import-backed overloads and direct exports remain eligible.",
