        "reason": "The independently reported metadata-parsing defects are #574 and #575. In #574, Annotated metadata such as '>1' inherits forward-annotation parsing incorrectly; the subscript visitor retains inherited context for the first type argument and enters NONE for subsequent metadata. In #575, nested typing-factory names and field labels are parsed as forward references; call traversal explicitly separates metadata from TypedDict values, NamedTuple field types, TypeVar constraints or bounds, and cast's type argument. #447 and #510 provide additional implementation and regression support for the same component-role boundary: Literal strings remain values, and cast's runtime argument remains ordinary data. This group overlaps the annotation-entry group for a different evidenced mechanism. Missing type names must still produce diagnostics, nested enclosing annotation state must be restored, structurally unsupported factory forms must retain fallback traversal, and metadata expressions must still receive ordinary expression checking.",
