        "reason": "Two independent defects occur when annotation-only metadata is given assignment-like effects on a prior binding. In #605, scope insertion replaces an ExportBinding and loses export-use information; the updater skips replacement only for an incoming Annotation when the name already exists. In #617, Annotation inherits a redefinition predicate that reports an imported value as redefined; Annotation.redefines is specialized to return False. The fixes operate at different owners because replacement and diagnostic classification are separate effects. Both preserve the existing valued binding, ordinary rebinding and value-bearing assignment behavior. #605 additionally preserves absent-name annotation insertion and annotation-expression use accounting. #486 is related infrastructure, but its postponed-versus-eager lookup policy is not the same replacement or redefinition mechanism.",
