        "reason": "These independent fixes correct opposite misclassifications at the same semantic protocol, Binding.redefines. #617 excludes value-free Annotation bindings because they do not define a name. #760 extends Definition.redefines to include a prior same-name Assignment, while retaining superclass classification. The common mechanism is subtype-owned definition semantics, not merely shared F811 terminology. The required effects differ: remove a false annotation-over-import diagnostic, but add the missing unused assignment-overwritten-by-definition diagnostic. Counterexamples rule out a blanket redefinition ban: ordinary assignment-to-assignment rebinding remains permitted, different names do not qualify for the added rule, and #760 does not implement the reporter's proposed class-body-only restriction.",
